mission "The Captain's Other Journal"
    name "The Captain's Other Journal"
    description "Bring the logbook to a shipwright who can identify the strange timber and copper fastenings."
    source "Puerto Cielo"
    destination "Port Azure"
    reward 1850
    speaker offer "Master Shipwright Edda"
    speaker visit "Master Shipwright Edda"
    speaker complete "Master Shipwright Edda"
    to offer
        has "The Wreck of the Saint Oria: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Bring the logbook to a shipwright who can identify the strange timber and copper fastenings.`
            `Master Shipwright Edda studies you for a moment. "The old sea charter settled one war, but it did not settle the past. The lost expedition sailed west under a sealed order, and its wake is stirring every ambitious captain in these waters."
            choice
                `(I will help uncover what happened.)`
                    accept
                `(Tell me what you are not saying.)`
                    goto details
                `(I have no wish to be drawn into another quarrel.)`
                    close
            label details
                `Master Shipwright Edda lowers their voice. "The maps were altered, the convoy erased from the books, and someone has been buying witnesses. Follow the evidence, not the flags."`
                choice
                    `(Then I will take the matter in hand.)`
                        accept
                    `(Not today.)`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Captain's Other Journal. Bring the logbook to a shipwright who can identify the strange timber and copper fastenings."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Master Shipwright Edda receives you at Port Azure. The evidence fits another piece into the puzzle: the expedition was not searching for gold alone, but for a place deliberately removed from every official chart.`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Master Shipwright Edda thanks you. "Every answer makes the sea less simple, captain. Yet the truth belongs to the people who live here, not to the first crown or company that can put a seal upon it."`
        log "Completed The Captain's Other Journal. Received 1850 gold. Bring the logbook to a shipwright who can identify the strange timber and copper fastenings."
